{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKhw3zAcMNL81xd1xuZ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Fix:** PR #743 (merged as `070fa8bc`, ticket RESTWS-1037) fixed it. The root cause is that `ConversionUtil.convertToRepresentation` returns the `PRIVILEGE_DENIED` sentinel when the caller lacks a resource's `getRequiredGetPrivilege()`. That sentinel was placed unchecked into collections, maps and nested lists, so Jackson received a bare `java.lang.Object` and failed with \"No serializer found\". The fix checks for the sentinel at each of those points. A collection or map containing a denied item is now replaced by the sentinel itself, and the enclosing property is dropped. `BasePageableResult` skips denied items in result pages instead of adding them.\n\n**Where it lives (current `master` line numbers):**\n- `ConversionUtil.java:67` defines the sentinel.\n- `ConversionUtil.java:364-373` (`getPropertyWithRepresentation`, collection branch) now returns the sentinel if any element is denied.\n- `ConversionUtil.java:397-406` (collection branch) and `:407-419` (map branch) do the same check.\n- `ConversionUtil.java:430-434` is where the sentinel is produced, when the privilege check fails.\n- `BasePageableResult.java:54-60` skips denied items when building the page of results.\n- `DelegatingResourceDescription.java:245-256` returns the sentinel from a collection-valued property, so the property is dropped.\n- `ConversionUtilPrivilegeTest.java:40-125` holds the new tests, which assert the sentinel is returned.\n\nPRs #744 and #745 carry the same RESTWS-1037 title and were merged on 2026-05-28, with different merge SHAs. They look like resubmissions of #743. I read only their metadata, not their diffs. I did not run the tests or reproduce the 500 locally.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"pr\": 743, \"repo\": \"openmrs-module-webservices.rest\"},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-module-webservices.rest\", \"commit\": \"070fa8bca3b59